  "full_response": "### **Infrastructure as Code (IaC)**\n**Infrastructure as Code (IaC)** is the practice of managing and provisioning computing infrastructure (servers, networks, databases, etc.) through machine-readable **definition files** (code) rather than manual hardware configuration or interactive configuration tools.\n\nInstead of manually setting up servers or using GUI-based tools, IaC allows teams to define infrastructure in **declarative** (desired state) or **imperative** (step-by-step) code, which can be version-controlled, automated, and reused.\n\n---\n\n### **Key Benefits of Infrastructure as Code (IaC)**\n1. **Automation & Speed**\n   - Eliminates manual setup, reducing human error and accelerating deployments.\n   - Enables **repeatable** and **consistent** infrastructure provisioning.\n\n2. **Version Control & Collaboration**\n   - Infrastructure definitions are stored in **Git** (or similar VCS), allowing tracking of changes, rollbacks, and team collaboration.\n   - Enables **Infrastructure as Software**—treating infrastructure like application code.\n\n3. **Consistency & Reduced Drift**\n   - Ensures that environments (dev, staging, prod) are **identical**, reducing \"works on my machine\" issues.\n   - Prevents **configuration drift** (unintended changes over time).\n\n4. **Scalability & Reusability**\n   - Infrastructure can be **scaled up/down** quickly with minimal effort.\n   - **Modular code** (e.g., Terraform modules, Ansible roles) can be reused across projects.\n\n5. **Disaster Recovery & Self-Healing**\n   - If infrastructure fails, it can be **rebuilt automatically** from code.\n   - Enables **immutable infrastructure**—replacing faulty components instead of fixing them.\n\n6. **Cost Efficiency**\n   - Reduces **operational overhead** by automating manual tasks.\n   - Helps **optimize cloud costs** by spinning up/down resources as needed.\n\n7. **Security & Compliance**\n   - **Policy as Code** (e.g., Open Policy Agent, AWS Config) enforces security rules automatically.\n   - Reduces **misconfigurations**, a common cause of security breaches.\n\n8. **DevOps & CI/CD Integration**\n   - Fits seamlessly into **CI/CD pipelines**, enabling **GitOps** workflows.\n   - Allows **infrastructure testing** (e.g., with Terratest, Check",
